186419941 1079 #uuid "fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419942 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419916 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419942 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419942 1077 "field-1" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419942 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419916 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419942 1079 #uuid "fea0be10-7e7a-5e8c-b225-cbbbd6502e43" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419943 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419930 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419943 1069 "q-210784" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419943 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419943 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{x}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419943 1072 #uuid "298016d0-4ea6-54d8-a832-231f3f8e4443" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419943 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 2,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}(1-\\frac{t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4})|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419944 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419928 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419944 1069 "q-126177" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419944 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419944 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{225}{(x+15)^{2}}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 5).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419944 1072 #uuid "3191d215-7e03-5aae-a424-72356e84e8e6" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419944 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{225}{(5+15)^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419945 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419934 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419945 1069 "q-89700" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419945 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419945 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-x}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(2<X\\le 4).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419945 1072 #uuid "3ffe741c-4355-5cb4-a113-2fae2e76fdee" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419945 1074 "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 4) & =P(X\\le 4)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(2) \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}-(1-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419946 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419932 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419946 1069 "q-89747" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419946 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419946 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21}, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(3<X<4).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419946 1072 #uuid "502fa5ed-8192-5239-85ce-b51fd4a6a69d" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419946 1074 "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<4) & =P(3<X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}-4}{21}-\\frac{{3}^{2}-4}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419947 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419936 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419947 1069 "q-89652" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419947 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419947 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419947 1072 #uuid "6056a54f-50c5-51bf-9c90-30d0151550be" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419947 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{6}{{t}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{6}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419948 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419937 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419948 1069 "q-89746" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419948 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419948 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-6x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(5\\le X\\le 8).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419948 1072 #uuid "83a3d348-6693-5dcc-af5c-61cd638a0bb7" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419948 1074 "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5\\le X\\le 8) & =P(5<X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8)-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(8)-F(5) \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-48}-(1-{e}^{-30}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-30}-{e}^{-48}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419949 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419931 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419949 1069 "q-89664" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419949 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419949 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{15}(6-x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419949 1072 #uuid "9853f7b8-7c5d-5c25-8113-542fa8b8a6a4" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419949 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{15}(6-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{15}t(t-12)|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}x(x-12)-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+12x-20}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{-{x}^{2}+12x-20}{15}, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419950 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419933 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419950 1069 "q-89631" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419950 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419950 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2x})},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419950 1072 #uuid "aa0570cf-0a8d-5b19-8cfc-d1d338d11235" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419950 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2t})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{t}}{\\pi }|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419951 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419940 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419951 1069 "q-89635" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419951 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419951 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{3}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419951 1072 #uuid "ae38bc39-2bd5-58c3-af2b-ad65de482c6d" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419951 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419952 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419939 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419952 1069 "q-89641" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419952 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419952 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8{x}^{4}},\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419952 1072 #uuid "b199a74a-63a2-5637-aa94-6d70ba2bd918" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419952 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2},$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x}\\frac{3}{8{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{8{t}^{3}}|}_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419953 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419935 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419953 1069 "q-89546" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419953 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419953 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419953 1072 #uuid "d87af21c-48b4-5612-ae7a-18902b89c926" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419953 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419954 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419938 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419954 1069 "q-210786" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419954 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419954 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{60}{x}^{3},\\, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419954 1072 #uuid "d8d29abd-ea88-5ad4-8655-fbf6ab67a44c" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419954 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{1}{60}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{240}|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{240}-\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{4}}{240}-\\frac{1}{15}, & 2\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419941 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1069 "q-210788" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1072 #uuid "dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419955 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419956 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419927 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419956 1069 "q-126213" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419956 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419956 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{4{e}^{2x}}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{3}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419956 1072 #uuid "dbdaccde-7824-5d29-93f1-f05b495a99f8" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419956 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{2x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419957 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419929 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419957 1069 "q-126176" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419957 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419957 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<4 \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>6).$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419957 1072 #uuid "de421a60-85ed-5a5a-9a98-5df02c4cb3f4" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419957 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-(1-\\frac{16}{{6}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419958 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419942 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419958 1069 "q-210762" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419958 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419958 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{e}^{-|4x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419958 1072 #uuid "fb64e84b-4036-56ed-b5be-3b99c498406f" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true] [17592186419958 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\le 0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals. \n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn particular, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{2},\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534347 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-04fc2411-0461-5350-a6d4-77130a96a596" 17592186419856 "answer-095360e1-dd96-5383-931f-a201eff47a39" 17592186419857 "answer-0b1e4645-ce48-5f06-a7d7-34323e0d0b93" 17592186419858 "answer-0e41de6f-5095-5ac0-a495-3d30c7145756" 17592186419859 "answer-0f9b63be-e003-513c-960b-dc0a6866add4" 17592186419860 "answer-12669211-70db-53f2-9325-6e1ec5835553" 17592186419861 "answer-14cb2e76-8027-5b58-bb92-91643b6d3815" 17592186419862 "answer-1608a6a2-ef7d-5264-a5b5-e47796062000" 17592186419863 "answer-170a0edf-da7f-5652-903d-c47b4ac8c342" 17592186419864 "answer-1d135339-50d4-589a-bbdd-9dfafdad32ca" 17592186419865 "answer-22307ec9-ce6b-54ac-8d2e-3cf6990bb045" 17592186419866 "answer-2e1f547c-1869-547c-823e-9966458b8f4a" 17592186419867 "answer-35abf0ef-ee66-53cd-a97d-5575de5686bc" 17592186419868 "answer-3713bbf7-8cf6-556f-9963-5d4f811dfef6" 17592186419869 "answer-38c41f81-53df-5e58-be19-db1d50a00fde" 17592186419870 "answer-3a8d1627-2737-5252-95ce-1a7d32a52868" 17592186419871 "answer-447da342-1533-5f2c-8730-3f4fcfb6eb1b" 17592186419872 "answer-4b0ae796-f204-5f28-ae72-68cb7f93938e" 17592186419873 "answer-4b6bc818-cf5d-5fbf-8f54-469f90018d9d" 17592186419874 "answer-4f0f787d-1687-5d7b-90fc-bcc440b2102f" 17592186419875 "answer-588e72ed-c4d3-5982-8daf-db7b4cfb2955" 17592186419876 "answer-5b78d2ad-1275-5369-9916-4ad050ea2a49" 17592186419877 "answer-5f215aa0-6421-5dd2-9e39-875332acba0c" 17592186419878 "answer-6127124c-024d-5286-8963-795ce40b1454" 17592186419879 "answer-6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" 17592186419880 "answer-65bf060c-f63e-58ca-b70b-edc87d24113f" 17592186419881 "answer-6d30549b-41ec-5746-94b1-bdf0fddb2247" 17592186419882 "answer-6f38d0bc-036c-5a3d-8b34-69100927b81a" 17592186419883 "answer-6fdf2e24-d0fd-503f-a916-289e0fb74567" 17592186419884 "answer-712de365-0023-5929-82ba-68a165ee7cd6" 17592186419885 "answer